{%- comment -%}
Outfit Builder catalog export. Section Rendering API endpoint — fetched by
assets/outfit-builder-engine.js as JSON (?section_id=outfit-builder-data,
plus &page=N for N > 1). Only IN-STOCK variants are exported. Clothing and
shoes also need at least one occasion: tag; purses and accessories don't
(the engine infers their occasions from the style in the title).
Unpriced guard (2026-10-11): a variant priced at 0 means "not priced yet" in
this catalogue and is never exported, so the builder cannot add a $0.00 piece.
Paging: collections.all paginates at 250 products. The <script> tag carries
data-pages="{{ paginate.pages }}" and the engine fetches every page, so the
export no longer silently drops products past #250 (the store passed 250
products on 2026-10-03).
Bundle guard: only two groups of product types are exported —
core  (bundle_types): clothing + shoes in "Outfit Bundle Eligible"
(gid://shopify/Collection/491236458658).
addon (addon_types): purses + accessories in "Outfit Add-ons"
(gid://shopify/Collection/491238260898).
The tiered "Outfit Bundle" discounts (10% at 3+, 15% at 5+, 20% at 9+) apply to both.
KEEP both lists IN SYNC with those collections' TYPE rules (and
bundle_types with sections/main-cart.liquid). The collections aren't
published to the Online Store channel, so Liquid can't read their
membership directly — hence the mirrored lists.
Slot "bucket" assignment:
- Handbags, or add-ons titled bag/duffel/tote/purse/clutch -> "bag"
- belts, sashes, waist/body chains                        -> "waist"
(the engine only offers a belt with a bottom that has belt loops)
- other add-ons (jewelry, scarves, hair accessories)      -> "accessory"
- Dresses / Sets                       -> "look"   (a complete single item)
- Heels / Sandals / Athletic Shoes / Flats / Loafers -> "shoes" (Flats/Loafers added v1.8.1)
- anything tagged sub:sets / subtype:sets / subtype:active / sub:jumpsuits /
subtype:jumpsuit (two-piece Gym sets, Jumpsuits, Matching Sets, Rompers,
Athleisure sets, etc. — regardless of product.type)  -> "look"
- everything else                      -> "top" / "bottom", using sub:/subtype:
tags (sub:bodysuits, sub:bras, sub:tanks, sub:crop, sub:blouses,
subtype:tops for top; sub:pants/jeans/shorts/skirts/leggings/skorts for
bottom), falling back to product.type for plain Tops/Bottoms.
Field contract (keep in sync with assets/outfit-builder-engine.js):
{ id, title, url, image, price, type, bucket, core, addon, lp, mt, occasionTags,
fa, gal,   (main-photo alt and photo set, only for products with photo-less variants)
variants: [{ id, size, color, price, image }] }   variant.price is in cents;
variant.image is that color's own photo (null when the variant has none).
variant.chip (2026-10-15) is the verified white-background "chip" for that exact variant, read from the
product metafield bonnamira.chips (JSON keyed by colour value; each entry lists the variant GIDs it covers
and the Shopify Files URL). null when no chip exists -> engine keeps the normal image/fallback.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign bundle_types = "Athleisure|Athletic Shoes|Bodysuits|Bottoms|Denim|Dresses|Enterizos|Flats|Gym|Heels|Jumpsuits|Loafers|Matching Sets|Pants|Sandals|Sets|Skirts|Tops" | split: "|" -%}
{%- comment -%}
addon_types mirror the "Outfit Add-ons (Purses & Accessories)" collection
(gid://shopify/Collection/491238260898). They count toward the 3 pieces
of the tiered "Outfit Bundle" discounts. They don't need
occasion: tags — the engine infers occasions from the style in the title.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign addon_types = "Handbags|Accessories|Earrings|Bracelets|Necklaces|Rings" | split: "|" -%}
{%- assign printed_any = false -%}
{%- paginate collections.all.products by 250 -%}
<script type="application/json" id="outfit-builder-catalog" data-pages="{{ paginate.pages | default: 1 }}">
[
{%- for product in collections.all.products -%}
{%- assign is_core = false -%}
{%- assign is_addon = false -%}
{%- if bundle_types contains product.type -%}{%- assign is_core = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if addon_types contains product.type -%}{%- assign is_addon = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- unless is_core or is_addon -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- if product.available == false -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign oidx = 0 -%}
{%- capture occasion_json -%}
{%- for tag in product.tags -%}
{%- if tag contains "occasion:" -%}
{%- unless oidx == 0 -%},{%- endunless -%}
{{ tag | json }}
{%- assign oidx = oidx | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if is_core and oidx == 0 -%}
{%- continue -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign bucket = "" -%}
{%- assign title_lc = product.title | downcase -%}
{%- if is_addon -%}
{%- if product.type == "Handbags" or title_lc contains " bag" or title_lc contains "duffel" or title_lc contains "tote" or title_lc contains "purse" or title_lc contains "clutch" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "bag" -%}
{%- elsif title_lc contains "belt" or title_lc contains "sash" or title_lc contains "waist chain" or title_lc contains "body chain" or title_lc contains "belly chain" or title_lc contains "corset" or title_lc contains "cincher" or product.tags contains "sub:belts" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "waist" -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- assign bucket = "accessory" -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- elsif product.type == "Dresses" or product.type == "Sets" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "look" -%}
{%- elsif product.type == "Heels" or product.type == "Sandals" or product.type == "Athletic Shoes" or product.type == "Flats" or product.type == "Loafers" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "shoes" -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- for tag in product.tags -%}
{%- assign t = tag | downcase -%}
{%- if t == "subtype:sets" or t == "subtype:active" or t == "sub:sets" or t == "subtype:jumpsuit" or t == "sub:jumpsuits" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "look" -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if bucket == "" -%}
{%- for tag in product.tags -%}
{%- assign t = tag | downcase -%}
{%- if t == "sub:tanks" or t == "sub:crop" or t == "sub:blouses" or t == "subtype:tops" or t == "sub:bras" or t == "sub:bodysuits" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "top" -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if t == "sub:pants" or t == "sub:jeans" or t == "sub:shorts" or t == "sub:skirts" or t == "sub:leggings" or t == "sub:skorts" -%}
{%- assign bucket = "bottom" -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if bucket == "" and product.type == "Tops" -%}{%- assign bucket = "top" -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if bucket == "" and product.type == "Bottoms" -%}{%- assign bucket = "bottom" -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if bucket == "" -%}
{%- continue -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} Figure out which variant option index is Size vs Color {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign size_idx = 0 -%}
{%- assign color_idx = 0 -%}
{%- for opt in product.options_with_values -%}
{%- assign opt_name = opt.name | downcase -%}
{%- if opt_name contains "size" or opt_name contains "talla" -%}
{%- assign size_idx = forloop.index -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if opt_name contains "color" or opt_name contains "colour" -%}
{%- assign color_idx = forloop.index -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if size_idx == 0 and product.options_with_values.size >= 2 -%}{%- assign size_idx = 2 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
Only default color to a fallback index when a SECOND option exists and
isn't already claimed by size — single-option (size-only) products have
no color dimension, and color must come out null for them. The engine
then falls back to colors named in the product title.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if color_idx == 0 and product.options_with_values.size >= 2 -%}
{%- for opt in product.options_with_values -%}
{%- unless forloop.index == size_idx -%}
{%- assign color_idx = forloop.index -%}
{%- break -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign size_key = "option" | append: size_idx -%}
{%- assign color_key = "option" | append: color_idx -%}
{%- comment -%}
Belt-loop hint from the description (used for bottoms and looks only):
"n" = elastic / drawstring / already belted, "y" = says belt loops,
"h" = button-and-zip or five-pocket waistband. Anything else: no hint.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign lp = "" -%}
{%- if bucket == "bottom" or bucket == "look" -%}
{%- assign desc_lc = product.description | strip_html | downcase -%}
{%- if desc_lc contains "belt loop" -%}
{%- assign lp = "y" -%}
{%- elsif desc_lc contains "elastic" or desc_lc contains "drawstring" or desc_lc contains "belted" or desc_lc contains "belt included" or desc_lc contains "pull-on" or desc_lc contains "tie waist" or desc_lc contains "tie-waist" -%}
{%- assign lp = "n" -%}
{%- elsif bucket == "bottom" -%}
{%- if desc_lc contains "button-and-zip" or desc_lc contains "button and zip" or desc_lc contains "five-pocket" or desc_lc contains "five pocket" -%}
{%- assign lp = "h" -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
Variant photo gap: when any in-stock variant has no photo of its own, also
export the product's photo set (url + alt) and the main photo's alt so the
engine can pick the photo whose alt names the variant's color. A photo is
never shown for a color it does not name (engine.resolveVariantImages).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign need_gal = false -%}
{%- if color_idx > 0 -%}
{%- for variant in product.variants -%}
{%- if variant.available and variant.price > 0 and variant.featured_image == blank -%}{%- assign need_gal = true -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} Skip a product with no purchasable (in stock AND priced) variant at all, so it never prints an empty variants list. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign has_buyable = false -%}
{%- for variant in product.variants -%}
{%- if variant.available and variant.price > 0 -%}{%- assign has_buyable = true -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- unless has_buyable -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- unless printed_any -%}{%- else -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- assign printed_any = true -%}
{
"id": {{ product.id | json }},
"title": {{ product.title | json }},
"url": {{ product.url | json }},
"image": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 | json }},
"price": {{ product.price | money_without_currency | json }},
"type": {{ product.type | json }},
"bucket": {{ bucket | json }},
"core": {{ is_core | json }},
"addon": {{ is_addon | json }},
"lp": {{ lp | json }},
{%- assign mt = "" -%}
{%- for tag in product.tags -%}{%- if tag contains "metal:" -%}{%- assign mt = tag | remove: "metal:" -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor %}
"mt": {{ mt | json }},
{%- comment -%} dc (2026-10-22): dominant colour for multicolour pieces whose title names no colour (metafield bonnamira.dominant). The engine makes it the primary family and multicolor the secondary. {%- endcomment -%}
"dc": {{ product.metafields.bonnamira.dominant.value | default: "" | json }},
"occasionTags": [{{ occasion_json }}],
"fa": {% if need_gal and product.featured_image %}{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: '' | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %},
"gal": [
{%- if need_gal -%}
{%- for img in product.images limit: 16 -%}
{%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}
{ "u": {{ img | image_url: width: 400 | json }}, "a": {{ img.alt | default: '' | json }} }
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
],
{%- assign chips = product.metafields.bonnamira.chips.value -%}
"variants": [
{%- assign vfirst = true -%}
{%- for variant in product.variants -%}
{%- unless variant.available and variant.price > 0 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- unless vfirst -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- assign vfirst = false -%}
{
"id": {{ variant.id | json }},
"size": {{ variant[size_key] | json }},
"color": {{ variant[color_key] | json }},
"price": {{ variant.price | json }},
"image": {% if variant.featured_image %}{{ variant.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
"chip": {%- assign chip_url = "" -%}{%- if chips -%}{%- assign vgid = "gid://shopify/ProductVariant/" | append: variant.id -%}{%- for pair in chips -%}{%- if pair[1].v contains vgid -%}{%- assign chip_url = pair[1].u -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- endif -%} {% if chip_url != "" %}{{ chip_url | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %}
}
{%- endfor -%}
]
}
{%- endfor -%}
]
</script>
{%- endpaginate -%}
